<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="015" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Generalize CallerPrincipalResolver into the module/widget framework + wire the BffDataverseClient widget-data seam (register per-module strategy/predicate)</title>
    <phase>P1 Module-host foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:010</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Core external-access BFF surface (tags bff-api/auth); brownfield generalization of shipped auth code; asymmetric-registration + CIAM byte-for-byte preservation risk.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-plane / architectural generalization of security-critical shipped code with CIAM-preservation constraint — opus per CLAUDE.md §8.5.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Core external-access BFF surface shared with teams-app-r1 (Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**); concurrent edits would collide; /conflict-check required.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Generalize the delivered CallerPrincipalResolver into a module/widget framework: introduce a per-module registration
    seam so each module (widget) registers its ICallerPrincipalStrategy (plane) and its Tier-2 record predicate, using the
    ready third-plane seam (one AddScoped&lt;ICallerPrincipalStrategy&gt; + a DeterminePlane branch). Also wire the
    BffDataverseClient widget-data seam: ensure each module's read-data endpoint group (the app-only, participation-scoped
    read path the client-side read-only BffDataverseClient IDataverseClient impl calls) routes through the generalized
    resolver + the module's Tier-2 predicate, so widgets get participation-scoped data without OBO. Handlers + the group
    filter stay untouched; the CIAM path is preserved byte-for-byte.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer + BFF auth engineer. Follow ADRs strictly. Minimal-API DI + endpoint-filter specialist; disciplined at brownfield generalization without regressing shipped behavior.</role>

  <goal>
    A module-framework registration point in the BFF that lets each module (widget) register { plane strategy, Tier-2
    predicate } over the existing CallerPrincipalResolver / CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter / ExternalCollaboration
    dual-scheme, without touching handlers or the filter — AND the per-module read-data endpoint path consumed by the
    client-side read-only BffDataverseClient (IDataverseClient impl) routes through that generalized resolver + the
    module's Tier-2 predicate (app-only, participation-scoped, no OBO). The CIAM path is byte-for-byte preserved; the
    full BFF suite stays green; publish stays ≤60 MB.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec FR-22 ("R2's remaining work: generalize the resolver into the module framework — register per-module
      strategies/predicates") + design.md §3 (reuse-as-is + generalize) + NFR-08 (per-module Tier-2 predicate is a
      pluggable contract). teams-app-r1 shipped CallerPrincipalResolver (ICallerPrincipalStrategy :147, CallerPrincipalResolver
      :166, CiamContactPrincipalStrategy :244, WorkforcePrincipalStrategy :328) + CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter :29 +
      AuthPolicies.ExternalCollaboration :42, 9761 tests green, CIAM preserved, publish 46.90 MB. The documented third-plane
      seam is: add one AddScoped&lt;ICallerPrincipalStrategy, XyzStrategy&gt;() + a DeterminePlane branch; handlers + filter
      untouched. This task turns that seam into a per-module registration framework. D1 (grade workforce rights by ADR-034
      role→level) lands in F3/F5, NOT here — P1 keeps flat Collaborate.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/Authentication/AuthPolicies.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/BffDataverseClient.ts (read-only IDataverseClient broker impl the widgets call — the client contract this BFF read path must satisfy; do NOT fork it)</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>010 (ADR-028 A3 — the canonical rule set for principal-agnostic module endpoints this framework implements).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">§10 BFF Hygiene: state a Placement Justification in the PR for the module-framework registration surface (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); run /conflict-check BEFORE the PR (teams-app-r1 shares Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**); do NOT inject AI-internal types.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Verify publish ≤60 MB compressed: dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/; report absolute size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline (state PDB convention).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">The CIAM path MUST be preserved byte-for-byte — the generalization MUST NOT alter CiamContactPrincipalStrategy behavior or the CIAM token validation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Per-module registration must keep the group-level ADR-008 filter model (route-group policies + endpoint filters); no global middleware.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Interface seam justified by ≥2 real strategy impls; register concretes; follow the ADR-032 Null-Object / asymmetric-registration discipline for any conditional service (bff-extensions §F.1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Add/update tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (+ integration KEEP-path); no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests; keep the suite green.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-010-di-minimalism.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
