      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/r2-coordination-response.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Third-plane seam" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs">Add one AddScoped&lt;ICallerPrincipalStrategy&gt;() + a DeterminePlane branch; handlers + filter untouched — the documented generalization point.</pattern>
      <pattern name="NFR-08 Tier-2 predicate" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/AccessibleRecordSetService.cs">ComposeAsync(principal, entity) is the pluggable per-module record predicate — the canonical worked example to generalize.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check against teams-app-r1 for Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** + AuthPolicies/DI before editing; record the result.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the shipped resolver + strategies + filter + ExternalCollaboration policy; map exactly how DeterminePlane selects a strategy today.</step>
    <step order="3">Introduce a per-module registration seam: a way for each module to register its plane strategy (ICallerPrincipalStrategy) + its Tier-2 predicate (over AccessibleRecordSetService.ComposeAsync), wired via ExternalAccessModule DI — using the existing third-plane seam shape, not a rewrite.</step>
    <step order="4">Keep CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter + handlers untouched; the framework registers strategies/predicates, it does not change the group filter contract.</step>
    <step order="4.5">Wire the BffDataverseClient widget-data seam: confirm/register that each module's read-data endpoint group (the app-only, participation-scoped read path the client-side read-only BffDataverseClient IDataverseClient impl consumes) resolves the CallerPrincipal via the generalized resolver and scopes rows through the module's Tier-2 predicate — no OBO, no Graph-pointer exposure, keyed on documentId/record id. Do NOT fork BffDataverseClient (client contract stays stable).</step>
    <step order="5">Add unit + KEEP-path integration tests for the registration seam (per-module strategy resolves; Tier-2 predicate applied; a widget read via the BffDataverseClient path returns ONLY the participation-scoped set; CIAM path unchanged incl. a negative Tier-2 case) in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/.</step>
    <step order="6">Run dotnet build + dotnet test (full BFF suite must stay green); verify no new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</step>
    <step order="7">Run dotnet publish -c Release; record compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline in notes; escalate if ≥+5 MB single-task delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If generalizing would alter the CIAM byte-for-byte path (CiamContactPrincipalStrategy behavior or CIAM token validation), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6/NFR-01 — the CIAM path must not regress.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish .NET</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ (module-framework registration seam)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ (per-module read-data endpoint group satisfying the BffDataverseClient read contract, resolver+Tier-2-scoped)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (registration seam + Tier-2 + BffDataverseClient-path scoping tests)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a module registered with its plane strategy + Tier-2 predicate, when a request hits its endpoint group, then the correct strategy resolves the CallerPrincipal and the module's Tier-2 predicate scopes the record set — handlers + the group filter unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the CIAM path, when a CIAM caller resolves, then behavior is byte-for-byte identical to the teams-app-r1 baseline (CiamContactPrincipalStrategy unchanged) — regression test green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative Tier-2: a workforce caller who merely authenticates receives ONLY their composed accessible-record-set (not all records) — negative test green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a widget read issued through the client-side BffDataverseClient read path, when the module's read-data endpoint group handles it, then rows are resolved via the generalized resolver and scoped by the module's Tier-2 predicate app-only (no OBO, no Graph pointers) — a non-participant caller receives an empty/denied set (negative test green); BffDataverseClient is not forked.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full BFF suite is green; no new HIGH CVE; publish ≤60 MB compressed with delta vs 46.90 MB reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">D1 (role→level grading) is NOT implemented here — P1 keeps flat Collaborate; the framework leaves the grading extension point in place for F3/F5.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (:166) + ICallerPrincipalStrategy (:147) + CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter (:29) — delivered by teams-app-r1; a third-plane seam exists but there is no per-module registration framework. grep: no Map{Module}Endpoints registration abstraction wiring strategy+predicate per module.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — extend the existing resolver via its documented seam into a per-module registration point; reuse-as-is + generalize (design.md §3). The seam itself is the only new surface; strategies/predicates/handlers are reused.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the framework, each new module must hand-wire plane selection + record scope by editing the shared resolver/filter, re-introducing drift and the asymmetric-registration risk §10 exists to prevent; FR-01/FR-22 "add a module = register" fails on the server side.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <notes>
    §10 BFF-touching task: Placement Justification in PR + /conflict-check (teams-app-r1 shares this surface) + publish
    ≤60 MB (baseline 46.90 MB incl PDBs). This is the FR-22 generalization point; task 016 registers Assigned Work as
    the first module over it, and D1 (ADR-034 role→level) is deferred to F3/F5.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load all &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt; before starting; follow the task-execute pre-execution checklist. Run /conflict-check before the BFF PR.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
